ical power so the vulcan powered  by the aircraft's on-board  electrical system quite a powerful one  for obvious reasons the mini gun powered  by a large battery there was a gatling  gun on a u.s navy ship experimentally  electrically powered and i believe it  was 1890 so none of this technology is  new and it's over 100 years old but  there's nothing better for very for  basically putting up a curtain of lead  whether that's defeating an incoming  missile  or trying to kill an extraterrestrial uh  predator  in the jungle  clutched in the arms of bill duke  churning up greenery and undergrowth  while trying to hit a cloaked alien  hunter this scene from predator may be  one of the most iconic scenes in action  movie history and is certainly one of  the most recognizable shots from the  minigun's time on the silver screen but  i'm sure you'll be absolutely shocked to  learn that its depiction in predator  isn't exactly  realistic many larger-than-life action  blockbusters have used this popular  trope of our muscular hero slinging  curtains of lead towards their foes with  a handheld minigun from dwayne johnson  and furious 7 through to arnold  schwarzenegger in terminator 2 but  weighing in over 40 kilograms not  including the power systems and  ammunition using a minigun handheld  doesn't seem all that feasible at least  not for your average joe all in all  according to some rough calculations if  you take the gun itself a battery to  power the thing and enough ammunition to  keep it firing for just a single minute  you're looking at at least  200 kilograms that is  1.88 dwayne the rock johnsons  this thing is simply not meant to be  held and even if you are as ripped as  arnold schwarzenegger or terry crews  there's a factor aside from weight to  consider immense recoil  as a huge fan of things like predator  and terminator 2 i have often wondered  whether it might be at all practical to  actually fire a minigun from the hip or  whatever some people have said tha