ay there and then drop back  down again they really step over the  line into into fantasy territory for the  most part if they're vaguely  realistically depicted it's because it's  a fixed section of a campaign or maybe  it's a mounted gun in a multiplayer map  and you are taking it over you're on the  door gun of a huey or something and  you're using it in situ we can then  start to see realistic depictions of  miniguns but then in my experience  playing playing certain games that allow  you to do that you don't really get the  sense of how devastating this thing  would be in real life because it's  incredibly hard to hit nothing with it  and the bullets don't have enough damage  overall maybe one of the less well done  guns in games but sometimes one of the  fun one of the most fun as well it's  rare that we see the minigun in movies  or games portrayed in a way that is  closer to reality than fiction but in  the case of a weapon that's larger than  life using a minigun is a virtual power  fantasy it's a tool used to inject a  heavy dose of action and an opportunity  for the players to let loose and wreak  some carnage when it comes to opening up  exciting moments for players or creating  memorable moments in movies does it  really matter that the pop culture of  the minigun is far from feasible do we  truly care that it would take a hulking  human being to carry as you may know i  am usually a sucker for firearms realism  in games but for the minigun it's a case  of fact versus fun and considering the  six spinning roaring barrels firing for  the side of fun i think we can all agree  to allow ourselves some enjoyment with  our virtual miniguns  thank you so much for watching this  week's episode of loadout if you enjoyed  it make sure you subscribe and like the  video and let me know either in the  comments section down below or on  twitter at a regular dave what else  you'd like to see a future episode on if  you want more video game weaponry  content you can wa